 36S  c  2002Li46: E=234 MeV {+37}Cl beam was provided from the VIVITRON        
 36S 2c  accelerator at IReS, Strasbourg. The target was 12-|mg/cm{+2} of       
 36S 3c  98.2%-enriched {+160}Gd backed by 40-|mg/cm{+2} of 99.47%-enriched     
 36S 4c  {+208}Pb to stop recoiling fragments. Prompt |g rays from              
 36S 5c  deep-inelastic products were detected by the EUROBALL IV array of      
 36S 6c  Compton-suppressed Ge detectors and an inner BGO ball. Measured E|g,   
 36S 7c  I|g, and high-fold |g|g coincidences. Deduced levels and the yrast     
 36S 8c  sequence. Compared with shell-model calculations in the sd and sdfp    
 36S 9c  spaces.                                                                
